  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RESTORING KEY HABITAT OF NEARCTIC MIG BI</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to address the threats to areas still available for dozens of neotropical migratory bird species in the Bosawas Biosphere Reserve (BBR), a priority &apos;Birdscape&apos; for the long-term conservation of neotropical migratory bird populations. The main objectives are to increase the availability of habitat for, and the diversity of, Nearctic migratory bird species in the BBR and to strengthen law enforcement and governance in priority conservation areas. Partners will work closely with local communities to restore areas degraded by unstainable practices and extensive cattle ranching, as well as to implement agroforestry and silvopastoral systems that will also improve local livelihoods and contribute to climate change adaptation and mitigation. This will be accomplished by signing Conservation Agreements with targeted communities, to restore 10,000 hectares in priority landscapes in the BBR, and improve productive management across 600 hectares. Partners will build local capacities for a better institutional and community-based governance, based on a robust monitoring system for direct measuring of impacts on Nearctic migratory bird communities, including the first Monitoring of Winter Survival stations in this region, with support and involvement of local institutions and authorities for community outreach and education. Lastly, they will train and conduct patrols to identify and deter illegal activities in priority landscapes for restoration in BBR, and support negotiations between communities and encroachers for their voluntary retreat from the illegally occupied territories. Overall, the project will impact a 10,000-hectare landscape in which they will develop migratory bird-friendly agroforestry systems, recover degraded pasture or deforested lands and increase protection to ensure long term changes in forest conditions.</narrative>
  </description>
